.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP 8
\fB0\fR
All checked configuration files and zone files are valid. Warnings do not change
the exit status. \fB\-h\fR and \fB\-\-help\fR print the usage text to standard
output and also exit with 0 (as \fBkarictl\fR and \fBkaridns\-dbloader\fR do).
.TP 8
\fB1\fR
Problems found: unreadable file, syntax error, validation error, or ZONEMD
digest mismatch detected. \fBdb\fR: an error in the database or its data, a
database that cannot be read with the rights of the loader, or a loader that is
not installed (\fBDB support is not installed\fR).
.TP 8
\fB2\fR
Usage error (a missing or unknown command, missing or too many arguments; the
usage text goes to standard error). Nothing was checked. Before this release a
usage error exited with 1. With \fB\-\-json\fR the document holds the usage
error (\fBusage.*\fR) and nothing is written to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Check Configuration File Syntax
.RS 2
.nf
karicheck conf /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf
.fi
.RE
.SS Validate All Zones Declared in Configuration
.RS 2
.nf
karicheck zones /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf
.fi
.RE
.SS Validate a Zone Using Its Configuration
.RS 2
.nf
karicheck zone example.com /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf
.fi
.RE
.SS Validate a Specific Master Zone Standalone
.RS 2
.nf
karicheck zone example.com master/example.com.zone
.fi
.RE
.SS Check the Zones of a Database
.RS 2
.nf
karicheck db /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf
karicheck db internal /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf
.fi
.RE
